                \.
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "composition+algebra#HurwitzTheoremSection"} composition algebra – Hurwitz theorem
          %h2#implications Implications
          %h3#real_spinor_representations_and_supersymmetry Real spinor representations and supersymmetry
          %p
            This classification turns out to closely connect to various other systems of exceptional structures in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinors"} Majorana spinors
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+geometry"} spin geometry
            are intimately related to the four normed division algebras, and, induced by this, so is the classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebras"} super Poincaré Lie algebras
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            (which are built from these real spin representations). For more on this see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+division+algebras"} supersymmetry and division algebras
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry"} geometry of physics – supersymmetry
          %div
